<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Routing Divergence Plots for all Models</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See Appendix <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Language Code Index ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Multilingual Routing in Mixture-of-Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> for language code mappings.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04694v1/images/qwen3_routingdivergence.png" id="A1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/226;" width="548" height="226" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.1: </span>Mean entropy-normalized JS-Div per <span id="A1.F1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OLMoE</span> layer for 12 non-English languages. This is the same plot as Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Multilingual Routing in Mixture-of-Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, simply colored for language labeling.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04694v1/images/olmoe_routingdivergence.png" id="A1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/226;" width="548" height="226" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.2: </span>Mean entropy-normalized JS-Div per <span id="A1.F2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OLMoE</span> layer for 12 non-English languages. We note <span id="A1.F2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OLMoE</span>’s poor multilingual capabilities. </figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04694v1/images/gptoss_routingdivergence.png" id="A1.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/226;" width="548" height="226" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.3: </span>Mean entropy-normalized JS-Div per GPT-OSSlayer for 12 non-English languages.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04694v1/images/phimoe_routingdivergence.png" id="A1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/226;" width="548" height="226" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.4: </span>Mean entropy-normalized JS-Div per <span id="A1.F4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Phi-3.5-MoE</span> layer for 12 non-English languages. Compared to the others, <span id="A1.F4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Phi-3.5-MoE</span> does not display the same U-shape, as the first few layers surprisingly have very low divergence, especially the first layer. We verified and saw that a small subset of available experts were being called for all languages in layer 1, which is behavior that requires further investigation.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
